{"title":"List of National MATHCOUNTS Teams","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The following 56 states, regions, territories, and government institutions run state-level <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MATHCOUNTS\" title=\"MATHCOUNTS\">MATHCOUNTS</a> competitions. The top 4 students from each state form the state teams that compete at the MATHCOUNTS national championship each year. On many of the pages below you can find links to state competition sites.\n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Alabama_MathCounts\" title=\"Alabama MathCounts\">Alabama MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Alaska_MathCounts\" title=\"Alaska MathCounts\">Alaska MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arizona_MathCounts\" title=\"Arizona MathCounts\">Arizona MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arkansas_MathCounts\" title=\"Arkansas MathCounts\">Arkansas MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=California_MathCounts\" title=\"California MathCounts\">California MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Colorado_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Colorado MathCounts (page does not exist)\">Colorado MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Connecticut_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Connecticut MathCounts (page does not exist)\">Connecticut MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Delaware_MathCounts\" title=\"Delaware MathCounts\">Delaware MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=D.C._MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"D.C. MathCounts (page does not exist)\">D.C. MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Florida_MathCounts\" title=\"Florida MathCounts\">Florida MathCounts</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Georgia_MathCounts\" title=\"Georgia MathCounts\">Georgia MathCounts</a></li>\n<